/-
# Elements of large breadth generate a finite p-group (Kourovka Notebook Problem 4.69)

Kourovka Notebook, Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 4.69 (J. Wiegold): let G be a finite p-group
with |G'| > p^(n(n-1)/2) for some non-negative integer n; prove that G is generated by the elements
of breadth at least n, where the breadth b(x) is defined by |G : C_G(x)| = p^b(x).
-/

module

public import Batteries.Util.ProofWanted
public import MathlibExt.GroupTheory.ClassBreadth

@[expose] public section

namespace MathlibExt.GroupTheory.BreadthGeneratorsPGroupKourovka4Problem69Wanted

/-!
Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka
Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 4.69 (J.
Wiegold). UnsolvedMath record UM-00700276 (`KOU-4.69`), dataset ulamai/UnsolvedMath v1.8.0.

The breadth of `x` is MathlibExt's `ClassBreadth.elementBreadth p x`, the base-`p` logarithm of the
size of the conjugacy class of `x`; in a finite `p`-group the class has exactly `|G : C_G(x)| = p ^
b(x)` elements, so this is the breadth of the problem. `G'` is `commutator G`. The bound `n (n - 1)
/ 2` is an exact natural-number division, since `n (n - 1)` is even.
-/

/-- Kourovka 4.69 (J. Wiegold): if `G` is a finite `p`-group and `|G'| > p ^ (n (n - 1) / 2)`,
then `G` is generated by its elements of breadth at least `n`; the breadth `b(x)` is defined by
`|G : C_G(x)| = p ^ b(x)`, here `ClassBreadth.elementBreadth p x`, the base-`p` logarithm of the
size of the conjugacy class of `x`. -/
def generatedByElementsOfLargeBreadth : Prop :=
  ∀ (p : ℕ) [Fact p.Prime] (G : Type) [Group G] [Finite G], IsPGroup p G → ∀ n : ℕ,
    p ^ (n * (n - 1) / 2) < Nat.card (commutator G) →
      Subgroup.closure {x : G | n ≤ ClassBreadth.elementBreadth p x} = ⊤

/--
Resolved true: Skutin (J. Algebra 526 (2019), main theorem, arXiv:1804.01745) proves that a finite
`p`-group `G` with `|G'| > p ^ (n (n - 1) / 2)` for a non-negative integer `n` is generated by its
elements of breadth at least `n`; the Kourovka Archive records 4.69 as proved. Source: E. I. Khukhro
and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka Notebook, 21st issue,
arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 4.69 (J. Wiegold); resolution: A.
Skutin, Proof of a conjecture of Wiegold, J. Algebra 526 (2019), 1-5, arXiv:1804.01745, main theorem
(abstract): if G is a finite p-group and |G'| > p^(n(n-1)/2) for some non-negative integer n, then G
can be generated by the elements of breadth at least n; Kourovka Archive, Problem 4.69: This has
been proved, https://arxiv.org/abs/1804.01745.
-/
public theorem_wanted generatedByElementsOfLargeBreadth_holds : generatedByElementsOfLargeBreadth

end MathlibExt.GroupTheory.BreadthGeneratorsPGroupKourovka4Problem69Wanted
